<title>INDONESIA: Astra 1996 net up to 469.45 bln rph.</title>
<headline>Astra 1996 net up to 469.45 bln rph.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>12 months to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>				(in billions of rupiah unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			    469.45 vs  370.93</p>
<p>    Earnings per share (rupiah)     404    vs  319</p>
<p>Non-financial services</p>
<p>    Total revenues		   10,980.72 vs 11,668.76</p>
<p>    Gross profit			2,230.28 vs 2,163.14</p>
<p>    Operating income		  1,066.45 vs 1,114.86</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		     582.72  vs 632.95</p>
<p>Financial services</p>
<p>    Total revenues		    1,303.61 vs  943.03</p>
<p>    Total expenses		    1,052.15 vs  765.97</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			248.75 vs  172.47</p>
<p>Consolidated results</p>
<p>    Total pre-tax profit	     831.48  vs  805.43</p>
<p>    Retained earnings		 1,538.39 vs  1,173.57</p>
<p>NOTE: The consolidated results were audited. PT Astra International is one of Indonesia's largest conglomerates, with interests ranging from vehicle assembly and financial services to agribusiness. -- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364</p>
</text>
